# Systematic Trading track: compliance checklist

Every requirement on the Gator Quant Hacks 2026 Systematic Trading track page, its shared deadline component, the home
page, Devpost, the Hacker Guide and the Participant Terms, and where the final paper or repo meets it. The numbering
(1–73) and wording follow `research/compliance/REQUIREMENTS.md`, which quotes each source verbatim; the live track page
was re-checked against it on 2026-10-03 (only the deadline strings had changed, 10:00 → 11:00 AM).

**Where things are.** Table, figure, section, appendix, calculation and page numbers below are read from the final
paper's LaTeX labels and source (`docs/paper/note.aux`, `docs/paper/note.tex`; kept in `results/paper/labels.json` for
a clean clone) and every number from `results/paper/numbers.json` ({{meta:n_numbers}} numbers, each with its
source file and key; built {{meta:numbers_utc}}) when this file is built (`bash run.sh docs`), so they match
`docs/NOTE.pdf`.

**The paper** (`docs/NOTE.pdf`; LaTeX via tectonic, built by `scripts/build_paper.py`; {{meta:total_pages}} pages):
§{{ref:sec:summary}} Summary · §{{ref:sec:hyp}} Economic hypothesis · §{{ref:sec:data}} Data and universe ·
§{{ref:sec:method}} Methodology · §{{ref:sec:results}} Results · §{{ref:sec:risk}} Risk management ·
§{{ref:sec:liq}} Liquidity and capacity · §{{ref:sec:limits}} Limitations and next steps (pages 1–{{page:lastmain}}) ·
References (from p. {{meta:refs_page}}) · Appendices: {{app:Calculations}} Calculations ({{calc:Sharpe ratio}}–{{calc:Capacity and volume share}}),
{{app:Everything we tested}} Everything we tested (Table {{ref:tab:A-all}}, p. {{page:tab:A-all}}), {{app:Robustness and extra figures}} Robustness and extra
figures (Figs. {{meta:app_figs}}), {{app:Records}} Records (pre-registration, deviations, every read of held-out data,
variant tally, sources, the forward test).
Main floats: Fig. {{ref:fig:teaser}} (p. {{page:fig:teaser}}; the vision work) · Fig. {{ref:fig:edge}}
(p. {{page:fig:edge}}; fast tier by month, v2 equity curve) · Table {{ref:tab:head}} (p. {{page:tab:head}}; the executable
copier first, then the causal camera policy at 0.5 / 1 / 3 s and the benchmark v2 (the fast tier's own fills), IS and
OOS: $/day, ¢/share, return, volatility, Sharpe, max DD, turnover, fees ×2; the CV benchmark on points that later
moved is in Table {{ref:tab:A-cal}}) · Fig. {{ref:fig:firm}} (p. {{page:fig:firm}}; a firm with a licensed
0.5 s feed: CV equity curves IS → OOS → fresh holdout) · Table {{ref:tab:risk}} (p. {{page:tab:risk}}; risk controls that
operated in the backtests vs those proposed for deployment). Appendix: the data table (Table
{{ref:tab:data}}, p. {{page:tab:data}}) · Fig. {{ref:fig:f2t}}
(p. {{page:fig:f2t}}; frame to executable order against the 3 s bar) · Fig. {{ref:fig:speed}} (p. {{page:fig:speed}};
$/day against feed delay).
Other deliverables: the video `results/viz/courtside_60.mp4` ({{meta:video_s}} s), the deck `docs/deck/courtside.pptx`,
the Devpost text `docs/DEVPOST.md`.

**Status:** Met · Partly met (gap stated) · Team (a person must do it) · Info (nothing to check).

