| 23 | Sponsor data optional; free public data allowed | Met | Public Polymarket and Kalshi APIs, Ken French, OpenTTGames, TrackNet |
| 24 | Holdout = most recent 20% or 2 years, whichever is shorter | Not met by time (disclosed) | The stored OOS is the last 20% of matches by start time (`src/tape.py`, pre-registered in `HYPOTHESIS.md` before any result): {{univ.oos}} matches ({{split.oos_share}} by match count) from {{univ.oosstart}}, {{split.oos_days}} days, {{univ.oos_time}} of calendar time and {{univ.oos_vol}} of volume. The organizers' latest 20% by time is the {{split.cal_days}} days from {{univ.timesplit}}; all of it was read before the corrected policies were frozen, so no untouched window meets the by-time rule (§{{ref:sec:data}}, §{{ref:sec:limits}}) |
| 25 | Set the holdout aside early and don't look | Partly met | Split coded before any result; everything frozen before the single v1 evaluation ({{reg.e02.utc}} UTC, frozen in `{{reg.e02.prereg}}`; `results/oos_peeks.log` line 1). Every later policy was designed after that evaluation, so its OOS figures are non-blind (§{{ref:sec:method}} "How we ran the tests") |
| 26 | Evaluate the holdout once, at the end | Partly met | Evaluated once for the frozen v1 hypotheses (Table {{ref:tab:A-all}}; H6 held as an observational result, the causally timed rules failed). v2, the copier and the camera policy were designed after that, so their held-out numbers are labelled non-blind (Table {{ref:tab:head}}); the registry's {{reg.n_newpol_oos}} OOS-informed strategy designs, {{reg.n_pres}} presentation choices and {{reg.n_mech}} mechanical corrections are in §{{ref:sec:method}} and Appendix {{app:Records}}. Blind tests outside the declared universe: unseen markets (v2, v2-safe: fail) and the corrected copier on {{x1.markets}} never-fetched markets ({{x1.c}}¢ {{x1.ci}}, {{x1.n}} trades: fail, underpowered). {{meta:fwd_label}}: {{fwd}} |
| 27 | Report the OOS result good or bad; report every peek in the note | Met | v1's loss, the blind-test fails and the doubled-cost loss are reported (Tables {{ref:tab:head}} and {{ref:tab:A-all}}); `results/oos_peeks.log` records each run that read held-out data; §{{ref:sec:results}} and Appendix {{app:Records}} list, from `results/provenance/experiments.json`, every design or headline choice and every defect fix made after an OOS look |
| 28 | Walk-forward tuning inside IS, with a purge gap | Met (disclosed) | §{{ref:sec:method}}: monthly walk-forward inside IS; wallets qualify on past months only |
| 29 | Lag every signal; trade next; point-in-time data | Met (disclosed) | §{{ref:sec:method}}: wallets qualify on past months only; the copier acts only on prints after the detection second (tapes stamp whole seconds), after the network leg, the venue's hold and the {{copier.lag}} s block lag, and fills past the recorded tape are rejected; the camera policy selects, signs and sizes each order from information before it; fills at the fast tier's own prints are labelled a benchmark ({{v2.secshare.is}} of v2's in-sample profit is in the detection second); §{{ref:sec:summary}}: the onset look-ahead found and fixed (D9) |
| 30 | Cost in bps per trade, justified | Met | §{{ref:sec:method}} "Costs": fee = r·q·(1−q) per share = 10,000·r·(1−q) bps of notional, r = {{fee.rate}}; worked example in Calculation {{calc:Taker fee}}; fees paid {{v2.is.fee_bps}} / {{v2.oos.fee_bps}} bps of notional for v2 and {{cv.fee_bps.range}} bps for the CV trader (`results/tier0/cost_turnover.json`); spreads paid as traded |
| 31 | Show costs doubled; say so if the edge disappears | Met | Table {{ref:tab:head}} and Table {{ref:tab:A-all}} rows (½ and 1 tick worse entry, fees ×2, all costs ×2); §{{ref:sec:results}} and the abstract say the OOS edge turns negative when fees double (v2 {{v2.oos.fx2.c}}¢; every CV cell OOS, best {{cv.fx2.oos.best}} a day) |
